//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                 WHAT THE PANEL CARRIES
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

T OutlinerPanelCarry       | OutlinerPanel.h | 45-57 | owning                    | -  | What the panel carries between ticks — presentation only, and the caller owns all of it. Only the counted span the artist can see is touched, and the visible position is a row ordinal resolved by count rather than a pixel offset the panel remembers on its own. A panel that mutated the relations where the click arrived would apply against a linearisation that is halfway rebuilt, and would bypass the sequence that undoes it. entry, and the drag in flight. None of it is a transaction and none of it is scrubbed. position. A row's ordinal changes whenever an enclosure above it collapses, which is the one event this carry exists to absorb; a stale ordinal would move the view on a collapse made elsewhere.
    has   VisibleOffset        float             [-]  ?
    has   Sought               TextCarry         [-]  ?
    has   ConfirmedCount       std::uint32_t     [-]  ?
    has   VisibleAnchor        std::uint32_t     [-]  ?
    has   CountedWhenAnchored  std::uint32_t     [-]  ?
    has   RowsPresented        std::uint32_t     [-]  ?
    has   AnchoredOccupant     OccupantIdentity  [-]  ?
    has   DraggedOccupant      OccupantIdentity  [-]  ?
    has   LandingOccupant      OccupantIdentity  [-]  ?
    has   ReorderOpen          bool              [-]  ?
    by    Api/TexturePaintSpecification.h, Source/OutlinerPanel.cpp
    note  🔴 `12` §7 and `14` §6: the rows are read through `RankIndex` and the relations are never read here.
    note  🔴 Every mutation leaves through `OutlinerSequence::Declare` and is applied at the next tick's ①.
    note  ⚠️ What is held here is what `14` §4.1 places beside the document — the visible offset, the search
    note  ⚠️ The anchor is carried as an **identity** and not as an ordinal, unlike `LayerPanelCarry`'s chosen

