F PresentOutlinerPanel     | OutlinerPanel.h | 92    | api,nonthrowing           | 🚩 | Presents one tick of the outliner into the rectangle the desk resolved, and declares whatever was asked. never learns what a row, an enclosure or a subset is. of its own would paint at the depth its band carried before a drag rather than the one it carries now, and the two answers disagree the first tick the band is moved. and a refusal raised per panel per tick would append to the register on a path that cannot arise.
    in    Theme           const ThemeSpecification&  [-]   read for the palette and the band extents; never held
    in    Area            const WorkspaceRectangle&  [px]  the interior the desk resolved for this panel, honoured exactly
    in    PresentContext  void*                      [-]   an `OutlinerPanelContext*`; a null context presents an empty state
    out   -               void                       [-]   ?
    post  every declared intent sits in the pending run; nothing was applied here
    by    Source/OutlinerPanel.cpp, Source/TexturePaintSpecification.cpp
    note  🔴 Matches `PanelPresentRoutine` exactly, so a workspace declares it into `PanelIndex` and the desk
    note  🔴 The rectangle is the desk's answer and this panel asks no second one. A panel that opened a window
    note  ⚠️ Nothing here refuses. `14` §7 puts the interface context's existence on the desk that calls this,

